Package: trianglewins
Title: Comparison Harness for Constrained Triangulation Backends
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Michael", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Runs the same planar straight line graphs (vertices and
    constraint segments) through several constrained Delaunay triangulation
    backends and measures the results with code that belongs to none of
    them: vertex and triangle counts, whether area and angle bounds are
    honoured, whether every input segment survives as a chain of mesh
    edges, constraint depth computed independently from the output
    triangles, attribute interpolation error, and time. Backends are
    'laridae' (CGAL), 'cdtr' (CDT), 'trowel' (spade) and 'RTriangle'
    (Triangle), all optional.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: grDevices, stats, utils
Suggests:
    cdtr,
    laridae,
    RTriangle,
    sf,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    trowel
